[2025-09-23 20:58:02,386][heimdall.core][INFO] - Cleaned output : entities:
  - name: Co-occurrence Types
    type: method
    description: "The different types of co-occurrences used in the ViCo method. These include object-hypernym (oh), object-object (oo), and context-context (cc) co-occurrences, which are calculated based on visual information from Visual Genome and ImageNet."
  - name: Object-Hypernym (oh) Counts
    type: method
    description: "The method for calculating object-hypernym counts. For each region in VisualGenome, increment X oa ij by 1, for each word pair (i, j) ∈ S o ×S a, and for all synset pairs (S o, S a) ∈ O × A. X oa ji is also incremented unless i = j."
  - name: Object-Object (oo) Counts
    type: method
    description: "The method for calculating object-object counts. For each region in VisualGenome, increment X aa ij by 1, for each word pair (i, j) ∈ S a 1 × S a 2, and for all synset pairs (S a 1, S a 2) ∈ A × A."
  - name: Context-Context (cc) Counts
    type: method
    description: "The method for calculating context-context counts. For each image in VisualGenome, X c ij is incremented by 1, for each word pair (i, j) ∈ S c 1 × S c 2, and for all synset pairs (S c 1, S c 2) ∈ C × C, where C is the union of all object synsets annotated in an image."
  - name: ImageNet Counts
    type: method
    description: "The method for calculating ImageNet counts. For each image in ImageNet, X oh ij is incremented by 1, for each word pair (i, j) ∈ S h 1 × S h 2, and for all synset pairs (S h 1, S h 2) ∈ H × H, where H is a set of object synsets annotated for an image in ImageNet and its ancestors in WordNet."
  - name: Co-occurrence Type-Specific Transformation Function
    type: method
    description: "The function φ t : R d → R dt that maps ViCo embeddings to a type-specialized embedding space."
  - name: Loss Function
    type: method
    description: "The loss function used in ViCo method: Here φ t : R d → R dt is a co - occurrence type - specific transformation function that maps ViCo embeddings to a type - specialized embedding space . b t i is a learned bias term for word i and type t."

